6862,7049,57960,3,17,16,13,24,20,3,817,9334,19515,323,279,5300,311,2182,1212,432,7049,57960,3,17,13,20,20,3,817,9334,19515,13,55923,6649,311,4582,5300,323,27854,304,279,5537,6839,304,279,13549,13,3555,374,279,2783,315,279,27854,323,5300,4362,311,6896,3421,279,3054,1939,58,6405,921,25643,551,7,15,13,17,17122,317,322,474,17047,280,7633,1188,15,11,15,29621,7,24,11,15,29621,7,24,11,17,29621,7,19,11,17,29621,7,19,11,20,29621,7,15,11,20,29621,7,15,11,15,3237,1502,445,19,379,5356,44970,17,11,20,701,45,317,1502,445,18,379,5356,44970,19,11,18,13,20,701,36,317,1502,445,20,379,5356,44970,21,13,20,11,17,701,45,317,1502,445,17,379,5356,44970,24,11,16,701,36,626,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nCarpet costs $\\$21.95$ per square yard and the padding to put under it costs $\\$2.55$ per square yard. Felix plans to install padding and carpet in the region shown in the diagram. What is the cost of the carpet and padding needed to exactly cover the room?\n\n[asy]\nunitsize(0.2 inch);\n//import geometry;\ndraw((0,0)--(9,0)--(9,2)--(4,2)--(4,5)--(0,5)--(0,0));\n\nlabel(\"4 yds\",(2,5),N);\nlabel(\"3 yds\",(4,3.5),E);\nlabel(\"5 yds\",(6.5,2),N);\nlabel(\"2 yds\",(9,1),E);\n\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"5f7f9d818e9ec502511301f4345eb37a9d3e2629f1f8e5682886f6460af8c9a6"},"seconds":32.49013686180115,"seed":462202375283318549,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to find the total area of the room and then calculate the cost of both the carpet and the padding for that area.\n\nFirst, we break down the room into simpler geometric shapes to calculate the area more easily. From the diagram, we can see that the room can be divided into a rectangle and a trapezoid.\n\n1. **Rectangle Area:**\n   The rectangle has a width of 4 yards and a height of 5 yards.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of rectangle} = 4 \\text{ yds} \\times 5 \\text{ yds} = 20 \\text{ square yards}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Trapezoid Area:**\n   The trapezoid has bases of 4 yards and 9 yards and a height of 3 yards.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of trapezoid} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (\\text{base}_1 + \\text{base}_2) \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (4 \\text{ yds} + 9 \\text{ yds}) \\times 3 \\text{ yds} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 13 \\text{ yds} \\times 3 \\text{ yds} = 19.5 \\text{ square yards}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Total Area:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total area} = \\text{Area of rectangle} + \\text{Area of trapezoid} = 20 \\text{ square yards} + 19.5 \\text{ square yards} = 39.5 \\text{ square yards}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Cost Calculation:**\n   - Cost of carpet per square yard: \\$21.95\n   - Cost of padding per square yard: \\$2.55\n   - Total cost per square yard for both carpet and padding: \\$21.95 + \\$2.55 = \\$24.50\n   - Total cost for the entire area:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total cost} = 39.5 \\text{ square yards} \\times 24.50 \\text{ dollars per square yard} = 967.25 \\text{ dollars}\n     \\]\n\nThe final answer is \\boxed{967.25}."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{967.25}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To solve the problem, we need to find the total area of the room and then calculate the cost of both the carpet and the padding for that area.\n\nFirst, we break down the room into simpler geometric shapes to calculate the area more easily. From the diagram, we can see that the room can be divided into a rectangle and a trapezoid.\n\n1. **Rectangle Area:**\n   The rectangle has a width of 4 yards and a height of 5 yards.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of rectangle} = 4 \\text{ yds} \\times 5 \\text{ yds} = 20 \\text{ square yards}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Trapezoid Area:**\n   The trapezoid has bases of 4 yards and 9 yards and a height of 3 yards.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of trapezoid} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (\\text{base}_1 + \\text{base}_2) \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (4 \\text{ yds} + 9 \\text{ yds}) \\times 3 \\text{ yds} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 13 \\text{ yds} \\times 3 \\text{ yds} = 19.5 \\text{ square yards}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Total Area:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total area} = \\text{Area of rectangle} + \\text{Area of trapezoid} = 20 \\text{ square yards} + 19.5 \\text{ square yards} = 39.5 \\text{ square yards}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Cost Calculation:**\n   - Cost of carpet per square yard: \\$21.95\n   - Cost of padding per square yard: \\$2.55\n   - Total cost per square yard for both carpet and padding: \\$21.95 + \\$2.55 = \\$24.50\n   - Total cost for the entire area:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total cost} = 39.5 \\text{ square yards} \\times 24.50 \\text{ dollars per square yard} = 967.25 \\text{ dollars}\n     \\]\n\nThe final answer is \\boxed{967.25}.","id":"prealgebra:410"}
